{
  "id": "playground-design",
  "term": "playground design",
  "definition": "Playground design is the way a play space is arranged, including its spatial layout, visibility, and placement of activity areas, which influences how children move, play, and share space. In school settings, design can increase or reduce unequal use of central areas by different age and gender groups by shaping what kinds of play are possible in different parts of the environment.",
